{"id": "EUVD-2026-49034", "enisaUuid": "28f8d8aa-ad83-3955-a3af-4304de742c1b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nudf: validate sparing table length as an entry count, not a byte count\n\nudf_load_sparable_map() accepts a sparing table when\n\n\tsizeof(*st) + le16_to_cpu(st->reallocationTableLen) > sb->s_blocksize\n\nis false, i.e. it treats reallocationTableLen as a number of BYTES that\nmust fit in the block.  But the table is walked as an array of 8-byte\nsparingEntry elements:\n\n\tfor (i = 0; i < le16_to_cpu(st->reallocationTableLen); i++) {\n\t\tstruct sparingEntry *entry = &st->mapEntry[i];\n\t\t... entry->origLocation ...\n\t}\n\nin udf_get_pblock_spar15() and udf_relocate_blocks().  A\nreallocationTableLen of N therefore passes the check whenever\nsizeof(*st) + N <= blocksize, yet the consumers index\nsizeof(*st) + N * sizeof(struct sparingEntry) bytes -- up to ~8x the\nblock.  On a crafted UDF image this is an out-of-bounds read in\nudf_get_pblock_spar15(); udf_relocate_blocks() additionally feeds the\nsame length to udf_update_tag(), whose crc_itu_t() reads far past the\nblock, and its memmove() through st->mapEntry[] is an out-of-bounds\nwrite.\n\nValidate reallocationTableLen as the entry count it is, with\nstruct_size().", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:49:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:38:23", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eeb0f3e193f8e523d03e4c9e084f6b4875f50e8e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a9b79a951cfd70a9d31ca01ae2d08a20bb730e9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d726135099313958f8975532a2e15322ff150ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7285276aa50d2839afb5957ffd491ad282dc8f72", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a219acb2ce674d99bbd1b7b35ed8c384dac7200", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/04f4599a9efb90992d072a814960edf0cd62805d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7f7774b9da0ef17b87bfa238cf966ad0b3376150", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3ec997bd5508e9b25210b5bbec89031629cdb093"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r2mg-8x37-x2q4", "CVE-2026-64322"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01c45281-9243-329b-98a7-3053db89d1da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.32.60 <2.6.33"}, {"id": "01ff1c70-53ca-3b9d-89c8-7fa5181b54c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1df2ae31c724e57be9d7ac00d78db8a5dabdd050 <2d726135099313958f8975532a2e15322ff150ce"}, {"id": "058f3444-0c1a-3bbf-b6a7-f74d98dee938", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b1c5701ad6b3e5d21d16f65475651cfaaa41e7aa"}, {"id": "0a4c479d-e3fe-3abd-8dfb-cbc61870ec79", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "169133bf-0b80-35ea-bc0f-40708d0d7663", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a9f1af04f086656246f30354fb4564ce3b08c4a0"}, {"id": "37f19e2b-7bd1-3940-8c20-0cfb56dbbe46", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1df2ae31c724e57be9d7ac00d78db8a5dabdd050 <7f7774b9da0ef17b87bfa238cf966ad0b3376150"}, {"id": "38fd94b4-1d1f-3d9c-8206-25b9bc00b7aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1df2ae31c724e57be9d7ac00d78db8a5dabdd050 <0a9b79a951cfd70a9d31ca01ae2d08a20bb730e9"}, {"id": "436dc46a-0bda-3429-bef9-3438ff7e8026", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.5"}, {"id": "46a1fec8-ef26-32f4-ae18-4db25c2027e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9ae30e324a96d0328a575329d7a95a09b3318601"}, {"id": "4c7d9860-427a-3fe7-b172-56c75501b21f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1df2ae31c724e57be9d7ac00d78db8a5dabdd050 <7285276aa50d2839afb5957ffd491ad